# Next.js 15 Patterns and Best Practices

## App Router Structure
This project uses Next.js 15 with the App Router. Follow these patterns:

### File-based Routing
- **Pages**: [src/app/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/page.tsx) - Home page
- **Layout**: [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx) - Root layout
- **Metadata**: Export metadata objects for SEO
- **Sitemap**: [src/app/sitemap.ts](mdc:src/app/sitemap.ts) - Dynamic sitemap

### Metadata Management
Always export proper metadata for SEO:
```tsx
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "Page Title | Paraguay Tech",
  description: "Page description with keywords",
  // ... other metadata
}
```

### Image Optimization
- Use Next.js Image component for automatic optimization
- Include proper alt text for accessibility
- Use appropriate sizes and loading strategies
- Consider WebP format for better performance

## Performance Patterns

### Font Loading
- Use next/font/google for Google Fonts
- Configure font variables in layout
- Apply fonts consistently across components

### Analytics
- Use Vercel Analytics as implemented in [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx)
- Include analytics in the root layout
- Monitor Core Web Vitals

### Static Generation
- Use static generation when possible
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use revalidate for ISR when needed

## SEO Patterns

### Structured Data
- Include JSON-LD structured data
- Use proper schema.org types
- Include organization information
- Add contact and social media data

### Sitemap Generation
- Use dynamic sitemap generation
- Include proper lastModified dates
- Set appropriate changeFrequency
- Include priority values

### Robots and Manifest
- Maintain [public/robots.txt](mdc:public/robots.txt)
- Include [public/manifest.json](mdc:public/manifest.json) for PWA
- Configure proper meta tags

## TypeScript Patterns

### Type Safety
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces
- Leverage Next.js built-in types
- Use strict mode configuration
- Implement proper error handling

### API Routes (if needed)
- Use proper HTTP methods
- Implement error handling
- Include proper response types
- Use middleware when appropriate

## Development Patterns

### Environment Variables
- Use .env.local for local development
- Prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ for client-side variables
- Use proper TypeScript types for env vars

### Build Optimization
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting
- Implement proper bundle analysis
- Optimize images and assets
- Use proper caching headers

## Deployment Considerations
- Configure for Vercel deployment with custom domain (paraguaytech.com)
- Use proper build commands
- Implement proper redirects
- Monitor performance metrics